      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>HOW TO USE</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>One folder, three possible jobs: cut out the background, add a watermark, crop to story size. Switch on the ones you want today and press Run: only those run. Here A and C are on and B is off.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"folder-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pick your folder</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ol><li>On <b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma</b>, click <b>Browse</b> and pick your folder, or paste the folder's path into the box.</li><li>Click <b>Pick images</b>, then <b>Select all</b>, or click only the pictures you want. The button shows how many are picked.</li><li>Press <b>Run</b> once. Leave the Run count at <b>1</b>: the node sends every picture through by itself, one after the other.</li></ol><p>\\n\\n</p><p>This workflow opens with <b>no folder picked</b>: choose your own folder, or try it first on the demo folder <b>Products</b> inside the <b>Media Inputs</b> folder that comes with these workflows.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;A folder inside ComfyUI's own <code>input</code> or <code>output</code> folder works straight away. A folder anywhere else works too, but pick it once with <b>Browse</b>: that is how ComfyUI knows you allowed it.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pictures go through in name order. Name them <code>01_</code>, <code>02_</code> and so on if the order matters.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"gear\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Using the switch</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>Click a row on <b>Mute Switch Pixaroma</b> to switch that step on (orange) or off (grey). The muted node greys out on the canvas.</li><li>Wire the LAST node of a step into a row, here the Preview of each step. Everything before it is skipped along with it, because ComfyUI never runs what nothing needs.</li><li>Add a step: build it, then wire its last node into the empty row at the bottom; a new empty row appears.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Mute (the default) skips a step completely. Bypass instead lets the picture pass through the switched-off nodes unchanged.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"question-mark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Something not working?</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Each button opens the answer on the Pixaroma help page.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-folder-not-approved\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Folder not approved</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-bg-models\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Which background model</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/look/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Nodes look different from the video</a></span>&nbsp;</p><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"How to Use\",\"icon\":\"to-do\",\"color\":\"#2a9d8f\"}}"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "note_json": "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>HOW TO USE</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>One folder, three possible jobs: cut out the background, add a watermark, crop to story size. Switch on the ones you want today and press Run: only those run. Here A and C are on and B is off.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"folder-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pick your folder</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ol><li>On <b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma</b>, click <b>Browse</b> and pick your folder, or paste the folder's path into the box.</li><li>Click <b>Pick images</b>, then <b>Select all</b>, or click only the pictures you want. The button shows how many are picked.</li><li>Press <b>Run</b> once. Leave the Run count at <b>1</b>: the node sends every picture through by itself, one after the other.</li></ol><p>\\n\\n</p><p>This workflow opens with <b>no folder picked</b>: choose your own folder, or try it first on the demo folder <b>Products</b> inside the <b>Media Inputs</b> folder that comes with these workflows.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;A folder inside ComfyUI's own <code>input</code> or <code>output</code> folder works straight away. A folder anywhere else works too, but pick it once with <b>Browse</b>: that is how ComfyUI knows you allowed it.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pictures go through in name order. Name them <code>01_</code>, <code>02_</code> and so on if the order matters.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"gear\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Using the switch</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li>Click a row on <b>Mute Switch Pixaroma</b> to switch that step on (orange) or off (grey). The muted node greys out on the canvas.</li><li>Wire the LAST node of a step into a row, here the Preview of each step. Everything before it is skipped along with it, because ComfyUI never runs what nothing needs.</li><li>Add a step: build it, then wire its last node into the empty row at the bottom; a new empty row appears.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Mute (the default) skips a step completely. Bypass instead lets the picture pass through the switched-off nodes unchanged.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"question-mark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Something not working?</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Each button opens the answer on the Pixaroma help page.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-folder-not-approved\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Folder not approved</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-bg-models\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Which background model</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/look/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Nodes look different from the video</a></span>&nbsp;</p><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"How to Use\",\"icon\":\"to-do\",\"color\":\"#2a9d8f\"}}"
