      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>WHAT EACH NODE DOES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The colour of a node tells you what kind of node it is. Nothing here needs changing except the blue ones.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The steps you set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Blue, and numbered. These are the only nodes you need to touch.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma (1. your folder)</b> - Point it at a folder and pick the pictures. Press Run once and it sends every picture through the workflow, one after the other. Its <b>filename</b> output carries each picture's name to the save node, and <b>index</b> says which picture it is (1, 2, 3 ...).</li><li><b>Mute Switch Pixaroma (2. switch each step on or off)</b> - One switch per step. A row that is OFF mutes the node wired into it, and everything feeding only that node is skipped too. <b>Multi</b> lets any steps run together; <b>Single</b> runs exactly one. Click a row's label to rename it.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The work</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Green. They run by themselves.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Remove Background Pixaroma (cut out)</b> - Step A: cuts out the subject with the BiRefNet model.</li><li><b>Text Watermark Pixaroma (your text)</b> - Step B: stamps your text in the corner of every picture.</li><li><b>Resize Crop Pixaroma (story 1080 x 1920)</b> - Step C: crops every picture to the 1080 x 1920 story size.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"checkmark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The result</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark red, at the end.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Preview Image Pixaroma (step A: cut out, saved)</b> - The end of step A: shows the cut-outs and saves them into <code>ComfyUI/output/On Off/No Background</code>. It is wired into row A of the Mute Switch.</li><li><b>Preview Image Pixaroma (step B: watermark, saved)</b> - The end of step B, saved into <code>On Off/Watermarked</code>. Wired into row B, which is OFF in the demo.</li><li><b>Preview Image Pixaroma (step C: story size, saved)</b> - The end of step C, saved into <code>On Off/Story</code>. Wired into row C.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"info\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Readouts</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark. Nothing to set: they show you what happened.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Run Timer</b> - The dark clock above the result shows how long the last Run took.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Nodes Info\",\"icon\":\"node-v5\",\"color\":\"#3d7cc9\"}}"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
